<section class="questions" id="faqs" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="heading"><p class="eyebrow">The things you might be wondering</p><h2 id="faq-title">Good questions.<br />Straight answers.</h2></div>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details>
    <summary>How is Buytiva designed to work?</summary>
    <p>The intended journey starts with a delivery destination, matches it to an approved service area, then puts the request and quote in front of the customer before any order is confirmed. Shopping and checkout are not enabled in this web release.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
    <summary>How are procurers reviewed?</summary>
    <p>Applicants verify their email and receive a reference for status checks. Applications are reviewed before access is granted. Approved applicants can finish setup through a private, single-use invitation.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
    <summary>Will I know the service fee before paying?</summary>
    <p>Checkout is not enabled in the current web release. The product is designed to show the complete quote and request the customer’s acceptance before a supported payment can begin.</p>
    </details>
    <details><summary>When can I download the mobile app?</summary><p>Official store listings are not published yet. We’ll add download links here once releases are available.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I apply to become a procurer?</summary><p>Yes. Use the procurer application form. Your application is reviewed before procurer access is granted.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does Buytiva serve every delivery area?</summary><p>No. The intended matching flow depends on approved, active procurer service areas. A public coverage directory is not currently available, so we cannot confirm which locations are served.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What can I do in the web app today?</summary><p>You can create a customer account, verify your email, apply to become a procurer and check an application’s status. Shopping lists, orders, messaging and checkout are not connected in this web release.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Why do I need to verify my email?</summary><p>Email verification confirms access to the address used for sign-in and helps protect account and procurer application flows.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What should I do if my procurer invitation expires?</summary><p>Invitation links are single-use and time-limited. Use the support options to find the available recovery path; do not share the invitation link with anyone.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Are the Buytiva mobile apps available?</summary><p>Official Google Play and App Store listings have not been verified for release. We will publish download links when the listings are live.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where can I ask for help?</summary><p>Start with the support page for current account, application and product help paths. A public support email or live chat endpoint is not configured for this release.</p></details>
  </div>
  <a class="faq-help" href="/support">More help options <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
</section>

